":"TMBbCDQG6bENJoQSST0XiA","name":"Brigtsen's Restaurant","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"8KnMSrMuTI2AtHZ2LOI8OQ","name":"Maurepas Foods","shared_categories":"Restaurants, Seafood","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"Zi-F-YvyVOK0k5QD7lrLOg","name":"Muriel's Jackson Square","shared_categories":"Cajun/Creole, Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"_Bi9kN_eR75G1eqIl7S3pA","name":"The Bulldog","shared_categories":"American (Traditional), Restaurants","shared_category_count":2},{"business_id":"kdqoDMuvyNedsouc1i33vQ","name":"Araña Taqueria y Cantina","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"JhpRI9m71ybWHkAqRdL0Tg","name":"The Avenue Pub","shared_categories":"Restaurants","shared_category_count":1},{"business_id":"AU-B663F3MPO7W-goWwwXA","name":"B Mac's","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0},{"business_id":"pKykk7lnD6Tf9wSzJYRyJA","name":"Starbucks","shared_categories":"","shared_category_count":0}],"text":[{"business_id":"dul6XjaCh1GgA-YHpuChUg","review_id":"NutybXnJJw7SJ1pODiQ9Vw","date":"2014-09-06T20:41:25","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.953188955783844,"text_excerpt":"This place is so so so good and is staffed by super nice people. We went here on a saturday afternoon and parked in the back. There were 2 large groups and a couple smaller groups but we were seated and helped right away. I got the small shrimp po boy and my boyfriend had the small smoked sausage po boy and we shared a basket of fries and two sweet teas. Let me tell you, both po boys were ridiculously good and huge for being smalls! Everything is fresh and comes out really quickly. I got a side of their house made remoulade and poured it on my po boy and dipped fries in it, it was that good. We were given plenty of refills and offered togo cups for our teas. Our meal came out to about $21..."},{"business_id":"dul6XjaCh1GgA-YHpuChUg","review_id":"LC-R08oCTN1PFNI3Mp0aNg","date":"2014-03-29T20:20:48","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9468460083007812,"text_excerpt":"I am totally impressed with Avery's. The buffalo shrimp poboy is the stuff of my dreams: fried shrimp coated in hot sauce (think frank's red hot) and topped with blue cheese? Get out of my head, Avery's. The roast beef was deliciously messy and was topped with a zippy horseradish sauce. You get a ridiculous amount of shoe-string fries for less than $2. I went for a quick lunch. When I saw that it was table service, I was worried I didn't have time, but there was no need to worry. The servers were very quick and notably friendly. What a great lunch option in Midcity. I can't wait to go back."},{"business_id":"dul6XjaCh1GgA-YHpuChUg","review_id":"jC01mUjATRzotYTa6mfr2g","date":"2020-06-18T19:34:43","stars":5,"text_representativeness":0.9440597295761108,"text_excerpt":"Avery's is hands down my favorite poboy shop in New Orleans. Having become famous over the years for their Buffalo Shrimp poboy, The Sandbag, the Fried Potato Salad, or the Stas burger - you really can't go wrong. We stopped in recently as they just reopened post the Covid closures to get the Buffalo Shrimp. Seriously, I dream about this poboy. Even the half is almost too much shrimp (if that ever could be a thing!) They're perfectly golden fried and tossed in a tangy house made buffalo sauce with a bleu cheese dressing. Best served fully dressed. Had to get the fried pickle chips too. The bread is so fresh and the crust is flaky. During normal times, they have an awesome cozy dining room..."}],"visual":[{"business_id":"dul6XjaCh1GgA-YHpuChUg","photo_id":"9OOJj7GqEJWgPia1344T8A","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/9OOJj7GqEJWgPia1344T8A.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.9089510440826416},{"business_id":"dul6XjaCh1GgA-YHpuChUg","photo_id":"WE_VdP2stzMCFPBjrjXkQg","label":"inside","image_url":"/photos/WE_VdP2stzMCFPBjrjXkQg.jpg","visual_representativeness":0.8998901844024658},{"business_id":"dul6XjaCh1G